+| - | Inbound adapter | use case only, no REST controller | The back office is a person or app, but the canvas doesn't describe an endpoint. Listed as a question rather than inventing one. |
+| **D1** | **Boundary exception: shared kernel with Rentals' `BorrowerId`** (user insisted, 2026-11-01; confirmed after the challenge at plan approval, 2026-11-01) | Accounts' domain uses `pl.wojtyna.dddtrainingv3.velocity.rentals.domain.bikestation.BorrowerId` directly as the `Account` identity: not wrapped, not through Rentals' api. Allowed scope: **only that one class** in package `pl.wojtyna.dddtrainingv3.velocity.rentals.domain.bikestation` (no subpackages, no other class of that package). | **Risk:** Accounts couples to Rentals' internal domain package. Any refactoring of `BorrowerId` or of the `bikestation` package (rename, move, extra field, validation) becomes a breaking change in Accounts, and the boundary no longer protects either language. It also creates a **code-level cycle**: Accounts depends on Rentals (`BorrowerId`), and Rentals is meant to depend on Accounts (it consumes Account Blocked), which contradicts the reference map's "No cycles" decision. Enforcement: one commented exception clause in `AccountsArchitectureTest` (outgoing rule) naming exactly that class; a `DECISION D1` comment in `domain/account/package-info.java` and in the `Account` class javadoc. **Challenge given (see below).** |
